          "why": "A mechanism that weathered a volatile week with only $4K in liquidations — versus cascade wipeouts on rival protocols — pulled in readers who have been burned by hard-liquidation spirals before."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Oracle-free and undercollateralized primitives",
          "why": "BAMM, 3Jane, and Clearpool each attack the same overcollateralization constraint from a different angle; readers are tracking whether any design can hold as real infrastructure rather than a one-cycle experiment."
        },
        {
          "source": "https://morpho.org",
          "thread": "Institutional DeFi credit markets",
          "why": "Maple's direct lending to Web3 firms and Morpho's $50M raise from a16z and Ribbit signal that crypto-native credit is attracting serious institutional capital, and the audience is sizing how fast that channel scales."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Silent and unreported exploit drains",
          "why": "An ongoing attacker quietly draining multiple protocols while projects stayed silent spooked readers who need to know which markets are safe before allocating capital."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "TradFi regulatory skepticism",
          "why": "European banking authorities explicitly calling DeFi lending niche due to AML and hack exposure gave readers a concrete benchmark for how far regulated institutional adoption actually is."
