      "rows": [
        {
          "dimension": "Smart-contract exploit",
          "level": "High",
          "note": "Multiple lending protocols — Onyx ($3.2M), Wise Lending, Baseline Markets — were exploited in a short window, with at least one attacker silently draining several markets before any public disclosure.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Liquidation cascade",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Traditional overcollateralized protocols remain exposed to hard-liquidation spirals during volatility; Curve's LLAMMA soft-liquidation model materially reduces but does not eliminate this risk.",
          "source": "https://www.curve.finance/llamalend/ethereum/markets"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Governance and risk-management capture",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Chaos Labs walking away from Aave's $5M risk mandate over V4 architecture disputes shows that parameter governance at top protocols can become politicized, leaving critical risk settings in fewer, less accountable hands.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Regulatory",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "European banking authorities have flagged AML risks in crypto lending; undercollateralized products integrating real-world credit scoring (3Jane, Clearpool) face the sharpest near-term compliance exposure as they most closely resemble regulated lending.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Liquidity concentration",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Decentralized lending TVL crossing $30B remains concentrated in a handful of protocols; a shock to Aave or Morpho would redistribute a disproportionate share of systemic risk across the ecosystem.",
          "source": "https://eco.com/support/en/articles/14800882-best-defi-lending-protocols-2026-tvl-rates-risk"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Oracle dependency",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Most major lending protocols rely on external price oracles for collateral valuation and liquidation triggers; oracle-free designs like BAMM are nascent and unproven at meaningful scale.",
          "source": ""
        }
